extraction_notes: "Nightbane RPG printed 68-69; the class rules continue onto printed 69, where the alphabetical power list also sits. P.C.C. STORED AS category occ, occ_group psychic, per BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F77 (declined) and the Born Mystic precedent; the P.C.C. is stated in restrictions. POWER LISTS: the book prints its own three categories - Sensitive, Healer, Physical - on printed 69, and its membership disagrees with the catalog''s for twelve names (six it files under Super). Each starting group and the class-wide gate therefore narrows the CATALOG categories (Healer is the catalog''s Healing) with only-lists that reproduce the book''s lists exactly. The level-up power ''from any category'' is read as any of the book''s three lists, so categories_allowed is their union, not the catalog''s whole Super/Sensitive/Physical/Healing sets. The four automatic powers (See Aura, Sense Evil, Meditation, Presence Sense) are left out of every pick list, since picking one again grants nothing. The Healer list prints a bare ''Healing'' that has no description anywhere in the Healer section (printed 83-84, thirteen powers); not stored. NAMES RESOLVED: Suggestion to Hypnotic Suggestion (survey D7), Bio-Manipulation to Bio-Manipulation (the evil eye) (its description heading, printed 78), Impervious to Poison to Impervious to Poison/Toxin, Increase Healing to Increased Healing, Object Read/Psychometry to Object Read (Psychometry), See the Invisible to See The Invisible. I.S.P.: M.E. + 1D4x10, +10 per additional level; the per-level 10 is also stated in level_progression because the formula carries no per-level dice. EXPERIENCE: the Ashmedai, Psychic & Sorceror ladder, printed 233; level 13 prints 225,920 as its lower bound, the same figure that ends level 12, stored as 225921. SKILLS: Speak/Literate in Native Language 98% is stored as the two catalog rows at 98. The 4 work/educational skills name no category, so every category the book''s skill list prints (printed 48) is offered, Military included - only the related list says Military: None. The book files Horsemanship under Pilot (printed 48), so the related Pilot +5% is given to Horsemanship: General. Hand to hand costs (one, two or three related selections) and the Medical double cost are in notes and not enforced. HIT POINTS AND S.D.C.: the page prints neither; the core rule on printed 36 is P.E. + 1D6 per level, and S.D.C. 3D6 for anyone without a military, police, detective or athletic background (1D4x10 for those). MONEY: 3D6x100 cash is stored; the 1D6x1,000 in possessions is in restrictions. EQUIPMENT: varies with background plus a basic car, pick-up truck or motorcycle - vehicle rows, not gear, so prose only."
