## Lore

Dark Day did more than open the door to an invasion from another world: it
also raised the psychic energy running through the planet. Thousands of ordinary
people who had only ever had the odd hunch or premonition found their powers
waking in a way nobody had seen before, and psychics who had already learned to
use their gifts found them stronger and more reliable.

A psychic can sense the supernatural, move the world with the mind alone, and
even heal wounds and disease. The same senses let them see the Nightlords and
their minions for what they are, which makes them targets. Hunted by a
government the monsters control, psychics hide, and look for company among
other outcasts such as the Nightbane. Many fight back alongside secret
societies, cults, the Nightbane and the Spook Squad; some sell their powers as
mercenaries or adventurers, and some still try to live quietly.

This class assumes a young, ordinary man or woman who has suddenly discovered
new abilities and may soon be forced to leave a normal life behind.

## GM Notes

**Inner Strength Points** fuel every psionic power, and each power states its
cost. A psychic who has spent all of them can do nothing more until rested.
Sleep or total relaxation restores 2 I.S.P. per hour. **Meditation**, automatic
for every psychic and costing nothing, restores 6 I.S.P. per hour and counts as
two hours of rest for the body (printed 67).

**Saving throws.** A master psionic, which includes every P.C.C., saves against
psionic attack on a 10 or higher, adding any M.E. bonus.

**Psionic attacks per melee** equal the character''s physical hand to hand
attacks. See Psychic Combat in the combat section.

**Ley lines.** Range and duration of psionic powers rise by 50% within two
miles of a ley line and double within a mile of a nexus. Damage from psionic
energy attacks doubles within a mile of a nexus; a ley line alone adds none.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-psychic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'nb-psychic';

